    "summary": "Market woes, mariculture growth, and scientific strides Maryland watermen are enduring one of the worst seasons in memory — not because oysters are scarce, but because a market flooded by reopened fisheries in Florida and Mississippi has caused prices to collapse. In contrast, Alaska's mariculture industry is booming, with permit applications tripling over the last decade and NOAA identifying 77 new farming areas. On…",
